==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|treat|ment}}. Compare {{cog|fr|traitement}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɹiːtmənt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-treatment.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|treat|ment}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The process or [[manner]] of [[treat]]ing someone or something.
#: {{ux|en|He still has nightmares resulting from the abusive '''treatment''' he received from his captors.}}
# {{senseid|en|medical care for an illness or injury}}[[medical|Medical]] care for an [[illness]] or [[injury]].
#: {{syn|en|course}}
#: {{ux|en|A '''treatment''' or cure is applied after a medical problem has already started.}}
#: {{ux|en|Cancer survivors who got radiation '''treatments''' as children have nearly twice the risk of developing diabetes as adults.}}
#: {{ux|en|The change is due largely to the increased availability of antiretroviral '''treatment'''.}}
# The use of a [[substance]] or [[process]] to [[preserve]] or give particular properties to something.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[treatise]]; a [[formal]] written description or characterization of a subject.
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=vii|text=Firstly, I continue to base most species '''treatments''' on personally collected material, rather than on herbarium plants.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|film}} A brief, third-person, present-tense summary of a proposed film.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[entertainment]]; [[treat]]
#* {{RQ:Homer Pope et al Odyssey|14|passage=Accept such '''treatment''' as a swain affords.}}
# {{lb|en|euphemistic}} [[harsh]] [[punishment]]; [[retribution]]
#: {{ux|en|He’s been a naughty boy, so give him a good '''treatment'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Even if you supported the socialist regime, your class background often meant you were going to get the '''treatment''' regardless.
}}

